ird  translation and saying that it flows  from three main sources you can  understand where this is coming from but  this is kind of a garbling up of things  desire emotion and knowledge now  why is this off emotion is actually a  terrible translation of thumos which is  often translated as anger the spirited  part of the soul another beautiful  translation the incandescent part of the  soul which you can find in the filo  kalia it's not emotion although that is  probably there because somebody  translates the passionate thematic part  of the soul or passion itself as emotion  wrongly desire so plato thought that we  have all sorts of desires  plural and you can talk about it in the  singular as well this is epithumia  desires for food for sex for all these  sorts of bodily pleasures right so that  that is indeed something that people are  driven by in the republic and then  knowledge episteme in greek no it's not  actually  what human behavior is flowing from more  reasoning or the rational part and you  can take all three of these together you  know as  the parts that plato is actually talking  about in his text but this is really  what should we say this is a hot mess of  a rendering i won't even call it a  translation it's sort of a bad summary  that somebody came up with of plato's  doctrine and i i think if we did enough  searching we could probably track down  the original of it and it's not totally  wrong right it does connect up with some  things that plato is saying but boy is  this misleading so that is definitely a  fake quote  what can you do in order to avoid  re-sharing fake quotes because nobody  out there i i hope is going to  deliberately create fake quotes but what  can you do as a responsible member of  whatever we're going to call the current  internet regime that we live under the  new republic of letters well the first  thing is anytime that somebody quotes  something and they don't give you the  source text you shouldn't in fact  exercise he